 Where Things Stand

  - Legacy registration stack lives under src/main/java/com/anastasia/Anastasia_BackEnd/controller/UserController.java:1 and src/main/java/com/anastasia/
    Anastasia_BackEnd/service/registration/MemberServiceImpl.java:1, while newer work sits in src/main/java/com/anastasia/Anastasia_BackEnd/modules/...; the
    split is what’s driving the confusion.
  - Payments is mid-flight: controllers and Stripe client exist, but the saga layer (src/main/java/com/anastasia/Anastasia_BackEnd/modules/payments/
    application/saga) is empty and the outbox → Kafka → accounting path is only half wired.
  - Notification wiring (src/main/java/com/anastasia/Anastasia_BackEnd/modules/notification/orchestrator/NotificationOrchestrator.java:1) is in place, but
    there’s no verification coverage and event sources aren’t consistently producing module events.
  - No database migrations are present even though JPA entities exist across legacy and module code, so schema drift is likely.

